    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a 2022 F-150 with a slipping issue. I've hooked up the scan tool and I'm seeing some really irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit during the shifts. What are the most likely causes for these kinds of pressure fluctuations?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit of your 2022 F-150 could be due to various reasons. It might be due to hydraulic fluid contamination, a failing pump, or issues with the transmission's pressure control valve. It's also possible that you have a flexible coupling that is worn or damaged, allowing air into the system. Have you checked the hydraulic fluid level and condition, and have any codes been retrieved by the scan tool?",
